From a81442a16044ce4e10e76c442f87b5f28a7a6f83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:12:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: passthrough backend: the host GPU as the only executor
 (EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_SOLE=1)

With EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_SOLE=1 (and _WORDS=1) Eglantine still parses every entry (macros, QMD
bookkeeping, program binds) but executes nothing: the Vulkan rasterizer's draws, clears, dispatches and
queries, the DMA engine's launches, 2D blits, compute release reductions and 3D query stamps return at
once, and the host GPU does them all, with its own semaphore releases on. So guest memory has one writer.

- Syncpoints: the puller's fence increment (and the 3D sync method, through the rasterizer) moves the
  guest value at once and the host value when the host GPU has run the entry (armed with the fence of
  the submission that carries it; the 3D method, which may run on the back's thread, waits for every
  channel's submitted work). A poller thread runs them and rings stale doorbells.
- Acquires: Ampere SEM_EXECUTE acquires suspend the channel as the other acquires do (they were checked
  once and passed); the host's copies of acquires are dropped, since the rest of the entry reaches the
  host only after Eglantine saw them met. An entry that waits at an acquire is submitted up to there
  first (OnEntrySuspended), so work before it (other channels' releases) is not held back.
- Present: the frame is read from guest memory (Layer::UpdateRawImage) once the host GPU ran what was
  submitted (WaitHost, at most 250 ms).
- ASTC: every header of a pool is transcoded (Eglantine's texture cache, which told which are sampled,
  no longer binds textures): MKW ~35k textures, 4.3 GiB.

MKW, SYNC mode: boot, menus and a race on the host GPU alone, no deadlock, no Xid; menu and race frames
complete (thumbnails, HUD, track); VRAM 1.8 GiB (Vulkan idle) against 6.3 GiB next to Vulkan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
